{"study_accession":"PRJNA991558","secondary_study_accession":"SRP447497","title":"Recombinant IL-1 RA in human Chronic lymphocytic leukemia cells in vitro","description":"Inflammatory factors that activate NFkB play an important role in the pathogenesis of chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) but are not addressed specifically by current therapies. Interleukin-1 (IL-1) is a master-regulator of inflammation that is inhibited safely in humans by the IL-1 receptor antagonist anakinra. Anakinra (K) was found to inhibit NFkB activity in CLL cells in an IL-1 receptor independent manner and had properties of an intracellular anti-oxidant in vitro. Overall design: Purified human CLL B cells were cultured with or without 300 microg/ml of anakinra for 48h before RNA was extracted and total RNA sequencing performed.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":6,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN36313376","study_accession":"PRJNA991558","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"Pt.3 K","description":"Pt.3 K","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM7549837","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-10-08","attributes":[["source_name","blood"],["tissue","blood"],["cell_type","CLL-B lymphocytes"],["treatment","300 microg/ml of anakinra for 48h"],["time","48h"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR25152749","experiment_accession":"SRX20904057","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Ion Torrent S5 XL","read_count":9504199,"base_count":1110922142,"first_public":"2023-10-08","experiment_title":"Ion Torrent S5 XL sequencing: GSM7549837: Pt.3 K Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN36313377","study_accession":"PRJNA991558","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"Pt.3 Con","description":"Pt.3 Con","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM7549836","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-10-08","attributes":[["source_name","blood"],["tissue","b